{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalLaplaceTransformUnique","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalLaplaceTransformUnique","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.QIntegralTransforms"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalLaplace.unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalLaplace.unique","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-laplace-transform-unique.lean#L41-L59","doc":"**Uniqueness of the categorical Laplace transform (proved,\nconditional on the shared `transform`).**\n\nThe categorical Laplace transform is the monoidal mate of `Δ_q`\nunder the Frobenius pairing; that property fixes the `transform`\nmap.  Two `CategoricalLaplace A` data with the same `transform` are\ntherefore equal (the monoidal-law fields are proof-irrelevant).\nReplaces a false / unchecked `Subsingleton (CategoricalLaplace A)`\naxiom. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:categorical-laplace-unique","label":"prop:categorical-laplace-unique","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-laplace-transform-unique.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}